# GENERATED by .github/workflows/ci-image.yml -- do not hand-edit.
#
# The CI toolchain image every Linux job in ci.yml runs inside,
# pinned by DIGEST so a run is reproducible: an image rebuild cannot
# change what an in-flight PR was tested against. `make
# ci-image-check` fails when bootstrap.toml or Dockerfile.ci move
# without a repin. A human lands each repin, not the weekly build:
# it pushes ci/repin-image and stops -- why is the "Push the repin
# branch" comment in .github/workflows/ci-image.yml. Until a repin
# lands, ci-image-repin-check is red on every PR.
#
# CI_APT_SNAPSHOT and CI_BASE_* are what the images were built
# FROM, and every non-weekly build reads them back (#1748), so a
# rebuild reproduces this package set instead of drifting off it.
